    "lead": "Short answer first, because that's what you came for. If your ebook lives only on Kindle, you don't need an ISBN. KDP will let you publish without one and hands the book its own Amazon number, the ASIN. Print is another story. Paperbacks and hardcovers need an ISBN for each format, and a few distributors, IngramSpark being the one our clients run into most, want one for the ebook too. And here's the part that trips people up on almost every call we take: an ISBN has nothing to do with copyright. Your book is protected the moment it's written down. Registering it with the U.S. Copyright Office is an optional extra, though a useful one. Below we walk through ISBNs, copyright registration and the Library of Congress Control Number (LCCN), with fees and rules as they stand in October 2026.",
