          "Say you're Dana. (Dana is made up for this post.) She wrote a 30,000-word guide for new dog trainers and she only wants it on Kindle. Dana needs zero ISBNs. KDP's [ISBN help page](https://kdp.amazon.com/en_US/help/topic/G201834170) says ebooks and low-content books are the only formats where an ISBN is optional, and her book is an ebook. Done.",
          "Now say Dana changes her mind six months later. She wants the ebook in Apple Books as well. Apple calls the ISBN optional too, though its metadata guide says having one helps with sales tracking and charts. Then she decides to go wide through IngramSpark. That changes things, because IngramSpark requires an ISBN for an ebook. If she's in the U.S., IngramSpark gives her a free one during title setup.",
