          "So why register at all? Three reasons, and the first one surprises most authors. For a U.S. work, you have to register before you're allowed to file an infringement lawsuit. Second, statutory damages and attorney's fees are only on the table if you registered before the infringement began, or within three months of first publication. Third, a registration made before or within five years of publication counts as prima facie evidence in court.",
