    "lead": "Here's a thing we hear on nearly every first call. \"I got one quote for $500 and another for $20,000, so which one's lying?\" Usually neither. They're just quoting completely different jobs. The cheap one is often a raw draft typed up to hit a word count, and the expensive one probably includes interviews, research, structural editing, a few rounds of revisions and files that are ready to go on Amazon KDP. So in this post we've tried to pull the 2026 market into one spot: per-word and per-project ranges from public sources, the six things that really push a quote up or down, what you tend to get at each price level, and where our fixed packages ($699 to $3,999) sit in all of that. That way you can budget off something real instead of guessing between two wildly different numbers.",
