          "Why such a massive spread? Because \"ghostwriting\" is really three different purchases wearing the same name. There's the draft-only deal, there's a managed writing project with editing built in, and there's the full package that ends with your book live on Amazon. Most of this post is about working out which of those a given quote is actually selling you.",
          "For rough ballparks (and please, treat them as rough), a short lead magnet of maybe 8,000 to 15,000 words often lands near $700 to $3,000, while your typical 20,000 to 40,000-word nonfiction ebook is all over that $1,500 to $15,000 range we mentioned. Go full-length, 50,000 to 80,000 words or so, and you're looking at something like $6,000 to $40,000-plus. Celebrity books and heavily reported projects start around $50,000, but that's a whole other world and we won't pretend to live in it."
