    "lead": "Finding a few people willing to read your manuscript is easy. Learning how to find beta readers who give you usable feedback, and then treating that feedback as data rather than a list of rewrite orders, is where authors lose months. It takes two skills: knowing where to look, and running a small system that produces clear answers before you spend money on line polish. This guide sets out that system for US fiction and nonfiction authors.",
