    "lead": "Developmental editing vs copyediting is less a vocabulary question than a timing question. A developmental edit asks whether the book works, while a copyedit asks whether the words are correct and consistent. If you pay for a copyedit first and then find that chapters need to move or go, you pay twice, because many of those polished sentences get cut. This guide explains what each edit covers, the right order, and when to hire each.",
    "cta": "Explore editing & ghostwriting options",
