          "Of all of it, the rights wording is where we've watched authors get burned. You're looking for language saying it's work made for hire (or that copyright gets assigned to you), that this kicks in once your last payment goes through, and that the writer won't be credited unless you want them to be. There's a line-by-line walkthrough in our [ghostwriter contract checklist](/blog/ghostwriter-contract-checklist-nda-and-rights) if you want to go deeper, and [does a ghostwriter own your book?](/blog/does-a-ghostwriter-own-your-book-rights) explains the law underneath it."
